/// United States 401(k) retirement plans.
///
/// A 401(k) is a tax-deferred account. Pay that goes in as a pre-tax deferral
/// arrives with no basis (`basis zero`), so all of it, and all of its growth, is
/// taxable when it comes out. This system caps what goes in each year, prices a
/// withdrawal before age 59½, and warns when a required distribution is missed.
/// `us` counts what comes out as income, and takes what went in out of pay.
///
/// A market gain or loss reaches the account through a place of kind `market`
/// (`2026-03-31 retirement = 24_600 USD via market`). That is a revaluation,
/// not a withdrawal: it changes what the account holds, costs no penalty and
/// counts as no income.
///
/// The figures are community-maintained data. Verify them against the IRS
/// (irs.gov, the yearly "COLA" notice) before relying on them, and correct
/// them in a pull request when they are wrong.
system us/401k

use us


/// An employer-sponsored retirement plan (IRC §401(k)).
kind 401k : tax-deferred
  basis zero
  liquidity 5d
  has employer entity

  /// Elective deferrals are capped for each person and calendar year, across
  /// every plan they hold (IRC §402(g)), with a catch-up from age 50 and a
  /// larger one from 60 through 63 (IRC §414(v)). Employer contributions do not
  /// count. This payment took the year's deferrals over the cap. Any excess must
  /// also be returned by the plan before April 15 of the next year, or it is
  /// taxed twice (IRC §402(g)(2)).
  ///
  /// To fix: ask payroll to lower the deferral, and have the plan return the
  /// excess.
  law deferral-limit
    on in
    when from is wages
    count amount as elective-deferrals
    let extra = if owner.age >= 60y and owner.age < 64y then super-catch-up[year] else if owner.age >= 50y then catch-up[year] else empty
    require tally(elective-deferrals) <= limit[year] + extra "401(k) deferrals over the yearly limit"

  /// Money taken out before age 59½ carries an additional 10% tax on top of
  /// the income tax (IRC §72(t)). This withdrawal is priced at that 10%.
  ///
  /// To fix: if an exception applies (disability, separation from service at 55
  /// or later, substantially equal payments, and others in §72(t)(2)), keep the
  /// withdrawal and mark it `!` with the reason.
  law early-withdrawal
    on gain
    when gain > empty
    when not to is market | tax-deferred
    require owner.age >= 59y6m else owe 10% * gain to irs by date(year + 1, 4, 15) as early-withdrawal-penalty "401(k) withdrawal before age 59½"

  /// From age 73, an owner must take a minimum distribution from a 401(k)
  /// every year (IRC §401(a)(9)). It is the balance at the end of the previous
  /// year divided by a divisor from the IRS Uniform Lifetime Table (Pub. 590-B),
  /// 26.5 at age 73. Nothing came out this year. The first one may wait until
  /// April 1 of the following year, and owners born in 1960 or later start at 75.
  ///
  /// To fix: take the distribution before December 31, or the shortfall is
  /// taxed at 25% (IRC §4974).
  law required-minimum-distribution
    each year
    when owner.age >= 73y
    when self.balance > empty
    warn total(out, year) > empty "no required minimum distribution taken this year"


// The elective deferral limit (IRC §402(g)).
// Notice 2023-75 (2024), Notice 2024-80 (2025), Notice 2025-67 (2026).
param limit
  2024 23_000 USD
  2025 23_500 USD
  2026 24_500 USD

// The catch-up for age 50 and over (IRC §414(v)).
param catch-up
  2024 7_500 USD
  2025 7_500 USD
  2026 8_000 USD

// The larger catch-up for ages 60 through 63 (SECURE 2.0 §109), from 2025.
// The 2024 row repeats the ordinary catch-up: there was no larger one.
// verify: the 2026 figure against Notice 2025-67.
param super-catch-up
  2024  7_500 USD
  2025 11_250 USD
  2026 11_250 USD
